<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s1">
  <p class="st-k rv">01 · Challenge</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s1">Many brands, one appetite</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Akij Bakers, set up by Akij Insaf Group in 2020, makes breads, buns, cakes, biscuits, cookies,
    wafers, snacks and chocolate under brands such as Bakeman’s, Funtastic, Hi5, Fast, Yum and Elano.
    The website had to present all of them as one premium company without losing the character of
    each, in both English and Bangla.
  </p>
  <div class="st-grid st-g3 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Need 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Craving appeal</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Visitors should want the product before they have read a word about it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Need 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Many ways in</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Some people look for a brand, others for a kind of product. Both need a route.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Need 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Trust beyond the pack</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Heritage, certifications, export reach, press and CSR all belong on the site.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-callout rv">
    <p class="st-bh">
      How might we make a large family of everyday bakery brands feel premium and appetising, while
      keeping every product easy to find?
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s2">
  <p class="st-k rv">02 · Research and discovery</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s2">Learning from food brands people crave</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    The brief named five reference brands. I looked at what each one does well and took a single
    idea from each, rather than copying any of them.
  </p>
  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Five benchmarks and what I took from them</h3>
  <ol class="st-list st-wide rv">
    <li><strong>Ferrero Rocher</strong> A chocolate-led hero with one prominent Discover button</li>
    <li><strong>Lotus Biscoff</strong> Telling the brand story through heritage and quality</li>
    <li><strong>Feastables</strong> A bold, distinct colour for each product category</li>
    <li><strong>Kraft Heinz</strong> Product grids that mix still pack shots with livelier imagery</li>
    <li><strong>Brew Tea Co.</strong> Warm, everyday scenes for bread and tea-time products</li>
  </ol>
  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Three principles that came out of it</h3>
  <div class="st-grid st-g3 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Food first</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Large, appetising photography carries the page; text supports it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Colour as a signpost</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Each category is recognisable from its colour before anything is read.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Premium, not loud</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Restraint in type and layout is what makes the photography feel special.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s3">
  <p class="st-k rv">03 · Defining the experience</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s3">Eight templates, one structure</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Every page shares a header with the logo in the centre, a language toggle and search, a page
    banner in a thin gold frame, and a footer with quick links to the main pages and brands.
  </p>
  <div class="st-stats st-wide rv">
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">8</p>
      <p>page templates, with an English/Bangla toggle on every page</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">6</p>
      <p>category themes built on one category template</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">3</p>
      <p>breakpoints: desktop, tablet and mobile</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-grid st-g4 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Homepage</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">An indulgent first impression that leads into every category.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Categories</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Every product category on one page, each with a way in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Category</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Brands and products in one category, in that category’s colours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 04</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Product details</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">The pack, its sizes and barcodes, and related products.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 05</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">About Us</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">The company, the founder’s legacy, its brands and latest TV ad.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 06</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Global Presence</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Export markets, the supply network and food-safety certifications.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 07</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Media &amp; CSR</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">News, TV ads and campaigns gathered in one place.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 08</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Contact Us</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">A short enquiry form with clear validation and confirmation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s4">
  <p class="st-k rv">04 · Key UX decisions</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s4">Six decisions that shape the site</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Each decision answers a question a visitor brings to a food brand’s website.
  </p>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision A</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">One category template, six moods</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          Every category page has the same structure: the brands in that category, a photo hero, a
          product grid with brand tabs, media coverage and more categories to explore. Only the
          colour and background pattern change, so a new category needs a palette, not a new design.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/akij-bakers-categories.webp' | rel }}"
